r prior activation are natural killer (NK) cells, which are part of the innate immune system and play a crucial role in surveilling and eliminating abnormal cells. This scenario highlights the importance of NK cells in preventing the unchecked proliferation of monoclonal plasma cells, underscoring their role in immune surveillance and the potential for immune evasion in plasma cell disorders.''' \n"], "raw_output": "Option: C", "error": null}
